{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ScreenStates’ pitch is “small, dependency-free, drop into any screen.” This article covers the three ways that’s kept measurable rather than just assumed: a CI-enforced size budget, an audited concurrency guarantee, and a documented rendering characteristic."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The binary-size budget","anchor":"The-binary-size-budget"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"CI builds "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift build -c release"},{"type":"text","text":" on every push and sums the resulting "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".o"},{"type":"text","text":" sizes for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStates"},{"type":"text","text":" target, failing the build if that total exceeds the budget committed in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".github\/binary-size-budget.json"},{"type":"text","text":". There’s no single linked artifact to measure instead — the library product is “automatic,” and nothing in the package’s own build graph links it standalone — so the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".o"},{"type":"text","text":" total is the closest deterministic proxy available."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A legitimate feature addition that grows this total past the budget isn’t blocked forever: bump "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxBytes"},{"type":"text","text":" in that file as part of the same PR, the same way a dependency lockfile gets updated alongside the change that needed it. The job never bumps it on its own."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The Task lifecycle guarantee","anchor":"The-Task-lifecycle-guarantee"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCollection"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refresh"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshCollection"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadWithRetry"},{"type":"text","text":" each store their running "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" in a private "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"currentTask"},{"type":"text","text":" property, read by "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/cancel()"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"type":"text","text":". Every one of those "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":"s captures "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"self"},{"type":"text","text":" as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[weak self]"},{"type":"text","text":", not strongly — audited specifically to rule out a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"self -> currentTask -> closure -> self"},{"type":"text","text":" retain cycle keeping a store alive after its last external reference is dropped."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In practice, a completed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" releases its closure’s captures on return regardless of capture style, so this mostly matters for a still-"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"running","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" operation: without "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[weak self]"},{"type":"text","text":", a store couldn’t become eligible for deallocation until that operation finished, even once every other reference to it was already gone. See "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation"},{"type":"text","text":" for the rest of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" lifecycle — cancellation, overlapping calls, and the automatic cancel-on-"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"type":"text","text":" safety net this guarantee supports."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Re-render characteristics of the default placeholders","anchor":"Re-render-characteristics-of-the-default-placeholders"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshError"},{"type":"text","text":" only ever go active once "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refresh(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshCollection(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" have confirmed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"type":"text","text":" is already "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":" — both fall back to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCollection(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" otherwise, which never touch either property. That means "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshError"},{"type":"text","text":" can never be observed alongside "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".empty"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"type":"text","text":", so none of the three default placeholders can ever be on screen mid-refresh."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A parent view that reads "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.state"},{"type":"text","text":" (via "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView"},{"type":"text","text":") and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshError"},{"type":"text","text":" in the same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":" — the pattern "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI"},{"type":"text","text":" uses for a refresh toast — still has its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":" re-evaluated whenever either changes, same as any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" property read in a SwiftUI "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":". This guarantee is about "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"which","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" placeholder that re-evaluation could ever affect, not about avoiding the re-evaluation itself: since a default placeholder is only ever on screen while "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshError"},{"type":"text","text":" are both inactive, that re-evaluation never has a placeholder to needlessly re-render in the first place — only whatever renders the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":" case could be affected."}]}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI"],"title":"Related Documentation"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/performance"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Performance","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Performance"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The binary-size budget, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" lifecycle guarantee, and the re-render characteristics of the default placeholders — what’s measured, what’s guaranteed, and why."}],"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore/loadCollection(_:)":{"title":"loadCollection(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatestore\/loadcollection(_:)","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"loadCollection","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"@Sendable","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" () ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12ScreenStates0A10StateStoreCAASlRzlE5Valuexmfp"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/loadCollection(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Like "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/load(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", but maps an empty result to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".empty"},{"type":"text","text":" instead of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":" — convenient when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Value"},{"type":"text","text":" is a list of items to display."}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenState":{"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstate","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"ScreenState","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenState"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenState"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The four canonical states of a screen: nothing to show yet, in flight,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"showing data, or failed."}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI":{"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/gettingstartedwithswiftui","title":"Getting Started with SwiftUI","type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","abstract":[{"text":"Drive a SwiftUI screen’s four states with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore/refreshError":{"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatestore\/refresherror","title":"refreshError","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"refreshError","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Error","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshError","abstract":[{"text":"The error from the most recently failed ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refresh(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshCollection(_:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"type":"text","text":" is left untouched by a refresh"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"failure — the last good data stays on screen — so this is the only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"way to learn a background refresh failed. Cleared at the start of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"next load or refresh."}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateStore"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","title":"ScreenStateStore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" holder of a screen’s "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", driving both"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI and UIKit consumers from a single source of truth."}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateStore"}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatestore","type